  "ownsLevel": {
    "confidence": "verified",
    "items": [
      "Changing any of the four rungs also needs four Netch Leather wrappers (ccbgssse041-netchleather.esl): `ccBGSSSE041_DLC2LvlRieklingMeleeFighter` 00088A (PcLevelMult 1 (10–30)) and `…MeleeDead` 0008B0 (level 1) take their template from `DLC2LCharRieklingMelee`, which draws them, without `Stats`; `…MissileFighter01` 00088E and `…MissileFighter02` 00088B (PcLevelMult 1 (10–30)) do the same through `DLC2LCharRieklingMissile`, which draws the rungs' missile copies. All four are listed below as list owners.",
      "`DLC2EncRiekling02Melee`, `03Melee` and `04Melee` use `DLC2EncRiekling01Melee` as their template but not for `Stats`: changing the Riekling does not change them.",
      "`ccBGSSSE041_DLC2LvlRieklingMeleeChiefDEAD` 0008AF:ccbgssse041-netchleather.esl (the dead Riekling Chief, a row) is a Riekling with no template and level 1.",
      "Every other riekling record (the `Missile` and `Thirsk` copies, the `DLC2TempleWorkerRiekling` records, the Riekling Chief `DLC2ThirskRieklingChief`, `DLC2RieklingRescuer`, every `DLC2LvlRiekling*` wrapper and the CC `…MeleeChief`, `…LvlRieklingMelee`, `…LvlRieklingMissile`, `…MissileDead`) carries `Stats` and follows its template or list."
    ]
